WEBVTT

00:04.444 --> 00:07.436
- Who wants more potatoes?
- Hit me.

00:07.614 --> 00:12.074
Uh, Chelsea, the way it's supposed to work
here is that Berta serves us dinner.

00:12.252 --> 00:13.344
I don't mind.

00:13.520 --> 00:16.080
Hear that? She doesn't mind. Shut up.

00:16.589 --> 00:19.057
We're back.
- Hey, how'd it go?

00:19.225 --> 00:22.353
Don't know what you were worried about.
Your son's a wonderful driver.

00:22.529 --> 00:24.759
Thanks for taking him, Mom.
He needs the practice.

00:24.931 --> 00:27.092
Mm, pork chops.

00:29.969 --> 00:31.061
What are you wearing?

00:31.237 --> 00:33.432
Grandma bought it for me.
Pretty cool, huh?

00:33.606 --> 00:36.541
- You made him dress up as a chauffeur?
- He loves it.

00:36.743 --> 00:41.077
- Don't get grease on that jacket, dear.
- Yes, Miss Evelyn.

00:42.315 --> 00:45.614
- Would you like to join us for dinner?
- Oh, no thanks, I had a late lunch.

00:45.785 --> 00:49.016
And she sent a piece of pie out
to the car so I could eat too.

00:50.023 --> 00:51.354
Anyway, I better get going.

00:51.524 --> 00:53.617
Well, thanks again, Mom.
Say thanks to Grandma.

00:53.793 --> 00:55.055
Thank you, Miss Evelyn.

00:56.462 --> 00:57.986
- Good to see you.
You too.

00:58.164 --> 01:00.530
Oh, I almost forgot.

01:00.700 --> 01:02.998
- Have you two set a wedding date yet?
- No.

01:05.905 --> 01:07.668
We haven't.

01:08.474 --> 01:10.135
But we're gonna.

01:11.344 --> 01:13.812
Well, it just so happens that
a client of mine...

01:13.980 --> 01:16.380
...schedules the weddings
for the Bel-Air Hotel.

01:16.549 --> 01:20.178
And she told me there was a cancellation
for the weekend of June 26th.

01:20.353 --> 01:22.719
- The Bel-Air Hotel?
- In June.

01:22.889 --> 01:25.790
- Charlie, the Bel-Air Hotel.
- In June.

01:26.226 --> 01:28.353
Yeah, I heard, wow.

01:28.528 --> 01:30.758
- What do you think?
- Gee, I don't know.

01:30.930 --> 01:32.761
We hadn't talked about a date.

01:32.932 --> 01:36.299
Boy, it's almost impossible
to get a June date at the Bel-Air Hotel.

01:36.469 --> 01:38.130
Thank you, Alan.

01:38.304 --> 01:41.102
Judith and I had to get married
at the Sportsmen's Lodge...

01:41.274 --> 01:43.037
...on the Wednesday before Thanksgiving.

01:43.209 --> 01:46.804
Yes,
I remember the Indian corn centerpieces.

01:47.447 --> 01:50.041
Oh, Charlie,
I've always dreamed of getting married...

01:50.216 --> 01:52.616
...at the Bel-Air in the garden
with the swans.

01:52.785 --> 01:56.414
Yeah, but keep in mind
those birds are vicious.

01:56.589 --> 01:59.524
They look pretty,
but they'll peck your eye right out.

01:59.726 --> 02:01.557
I thought
if we had the wedding here...

02:01.728 --> 02:04.390
...the money we save could pay
for a nice long honeymoon.

02:04.931 --> 02:07.866
Yeah, I guess that's probably smarter.

02:08.034 --> 02:09.092
Shame on you, Charles.

02:09.269 --> 02:11.999
Depriving your fiancée
of her dream wedding.

02:12.171 --> 02:14.469
Especially considering
all the money you blew...

02:14.641 --> 02:17.166
...on hooch and whores
over the years.

02:18.878 --> 02:20.903
Thank you, Berta.

02:21.080 --> 02:25.540
Tell you what, the wedding at the Bel-Air
will be my gift to you.

02:26.152 --> 02:27.346
Are you serious?

02:27.520 --> 02:30.512
Gee, Mom, thanks,
but that's a little too generous.

02:30.690 --> 02:33.352
A little? All she gave Judith and me
was a dinette set.

02:33.526 --> 02:37.155
- Who's eating on that dinette set now?
- That's not the point.

02:37.363 --> 02:40.025
Charlie's marriage
is just as likely to fail as mine was.

02:40.500 --> 02:42.331
Thanks again, bro.

02:42.502 --> 02:44.970
Anyway, I asked them
to hold the date for 24 hours.

02:45.138 --> 02:49.040
- So you can talk it over and decide.
- Thank you, Evelyn. That is so sweet.

02:49.208 --> 02:51.301
Well, I do have an ulterior motive.

02:51.477 --> 02:54.344
The sooner you get married,
the sooner I'll have more grandchildren.

02:54.514 --> 02:57.540
Why, does Miss Evelyn
need a cook and a butler too?

03:00.053 --> 03:02.886
- Let me know, dear.
- I will.

03:03.690 --> 03:06.591
- The Bel-Air Hotel.
- In June.

03:08.461 --> 03:10.793
Let's see you get out of this one,
Houdini.

03:22.809 --> 03:24.970
So have you thought
about your mother's offer?

03:25.144 --> 03:27.476
Yeah, I have.

03:27.947 --> 03:30.040
I've got one question.

03:30.216 --> 03:31.774
Why June?

03:31.951 --> 03:35.546
What's wrong with getting married
in July, or the following October?

03:37.390 --> 03:39.585
October is a perfectly good month.

03:39.759 --> 03:43.718
Birds all fly south, so you don't have
to worry about swan attacks.

03:45.231 --> 03:47.995
Charlie, if you don't wanna get married
in June, we don't have to.

03:48.167 --> 03:49.429
What? No, no, no.

03:49.602 --> 03:53.732
That's not what I'm saying at all.
Where do you get this stuff?

03:55.775 --> 03:57.675
- So?
- So, what?

03:58.277 --> 04:00.871
Do you want to get married in June?

04:01.047 --> 04:03.174
Oh, we're back on that.

04:05.985 --> 04:09.921
Well, I can't think
of any good reason why not.

04:10.089 --> 04:12.455
And believe me, I'm trying.

04:12.625 --> 04:14.092
So that's it?

04:14.260 --> 04:17.093
We're getting married June 26th
at the Bel-Air Hotel?

04:18.431 --> 04:19.523
I guess so.

04:19.699 --> 04:22.133
Oh, Charlie, I'm so happy.

04:22.301 --> 04:26.203
That's only because you don't have
a swan beak in your eye socket yet.

04:27.573 --> 04:30.542
I'm gonna call your mom, then my mom
and then all my friends.

04:30.710 --> 04:32.075
Good, good.

04:32.245 --> 04:34.907
Alan, we're gonna do it.
June 26th at the Bel-Air Hotel.

04:35.081 --> 04:39.108
Oh, my God! Oh, my God!
Oh, my God! That is so wonderful.

04:39.285 --> 04:41.651
I know, I've gotta go call everybody.

04:43.589 --> 04:45.955
Congratulations.

04:46.626 --> 04:50.357
- Thanks.
- Wow, the end of an era.

04:51.164 --> 04:53.826
- Guess so.
- Well, you had a good run.

04:55.601 --> 04:58.365
- Yep.
- But now it's over.

04:59.105 --> 05:01.300
Forever.

05:03.309 --> 05:06.642
Nothing's gonna change, Alan.
Sure, I'm gonna be married.

05:06.813 --> 05:10.078
But I'm still the same guy living in the same
house with the same woman.

05:10.249 --> 05:12.342
Yes, yes, the same woman.

05:12.518 --> 05:14.418
Forever.

05:16.155 --> 05:17.884
Hey, can I be the best man?

05:18.057 --> 05:20.355
You'll need a sex change.

05:22.128 --> 05:24.358
- Where you going?
- Out for a drink.

05:24.530 --> 05:27.988
- Well, you can drink here.
- I could, but I don't wanna vomit here.

05:28.901 --> 05:31.096
Wait, wait, wait, I'll go with you.

05:31.270 --> 05:33.135
- Why?
- I'm not done poking at you.

05:34.507 --> 05:36.702
Hey, shouldn't you ask
the old ball and chain first?

05:36.876 --> 05:38.309
I don't need her permission.

05:38.478 --> 05:40.639
- Really?
- Yes, really.

05:44.450 --> 05:48.386
Although it is considerate
to let your partner know your plans...

05:48.554 --> 05:50.215
...so she won't worry.

05:50.389 --> 05:52.687
Sweetie,
I'm going out for a drink with Alan, okay?

05:52.859 --> 05:56.989
Sure, have fun.
- Thanks, love you.

05:59.432 --> 06:01.024
Shut up.

06:03.236 --> 06:05.466
- You're driving.
- Wow.

06:07.440 --> 06:10.068
Jake has one big-ass head.

06:12.411 --> 06:15.710
All kidding aside, she's a great girl
and I'm sure you'll be very happy.

06:15.882 --> 06:16.974
Thanks.

06:17.550 --> 06:19.984
Forever.

06:20.786 --> 06:23.687
- Are you done poking?
- For the moment.

06:24.891 --> 06:28.520
Boy, who would've figured of the two of us,
I'd end up being the carefree bachelor?

06:29.328 --> 06:31.489
If by carefree
you mean broke and lonely...

06:31.697 --> 06:33.824
...everybody would've figured.

06:36.435 --> 06:38.426
- Hi.
- Hi.

06:38.604 --> 06:40.663
- Charlie.
- Betsy.

06:40.840 --> 06:44.708
- I'm getting married on June 26th.
- Good for you.

06:44.877 --> 06:48.404
- At the Bel-Air Hotel.
- Nice.

06:49.782 --> 06:52.774
That means no matter how easy you are,
I can't sleep with you.

06:54.287 --> 06:57.188
I can. I'm Alan.

06:57.990 --> 06:59.855
Can he buy you a drink?

07:04.764 --> 07:07.756
- What you watching?
- Oh. Golf.

07:09.001 --> 07:12.459
- Don't sneak up on a guy, all right?
- Sorry.

07:12.638 --> 07:14.970
Your dad watches a lot of golf too.

07:16.275 --> 07:19.403
So listen, how'd you like
to be a groomsman in the wedding?

07:19.579 --> 07:20.876
What do I gotta do?

07:21.047 --> 07:23.106
You just walk down the aisle
with the bridesmaids...

07:23.282 --> 07:25.876
...and stand with Charlie
during the ceremony.

07:26.652 --> 07:28.950
Tell me more about the bridesmaids.

07:29.121 --> 07:31.783
- They're friends of mine.
- So they're old.

07:32.758 --> 07:36.717
No, not all of them.
I have a niece who's about your age.

07:36.896 --> 07:39.091
- Is she pretty?
- I think she's cute.

07:39.265 --> 07:41.130
Okay, I know what that means.

07:43.336 --> 07:46.169
- She's not a brainiac, is she?
- What does that mean?

07:46.339 --> 07:50.435
Well, I don't like them stupid, but I don't
like them talking down to me either.

07:50.610 --> 07:53.807
- Got it.
- And I like a little junk in the trunk.

07:54.847 --> 07:56.178
You won't be disappointed.

07:56.349 --> 07:59.284
- All right, I'm in.
- Great.

08:00.720 --> 08:03.518
You know, of all the women my uncle's
been with, you're my favorite.

08:03.689 --> 08:04.986
Oh, thank you.

08:05.157 --> 08:08.149
- And there's been a lot.
- I know.

08:08.327 --> 08:11.592
- A whole lot.
- Right.

08:11.797 --> 08:14.527
Like I'm betting around a thousand.

08:15.368 --> 08:16.562
Uh-huh.

08:16.736 --> 08:19.830
And that's just since
I've been old enough to pay attention.

08:20.006 --> 08:21.030
No kidding.

08:21.207 --> 08:22.401
When I first got here...

08:22.575 --> 08:25.544
...he told me that they were coming over
to water the plants.

08:25.878 --> 08:29.780
And I believed him. What did I know?

08:30.316 --> 08:31.681
Sure, you were young.

08:31.851 --> 08:34.843
And naive too.
We didn't even have any plants.

08:35.888 --> 08:38.652
- And there were some crazy ones too.
- I'll bet.

08:39.859 --> 08:43.317
Your niece doesn't have a license
to carry a concealed weapon, does she?

08:44.263 --> 08:46.925
- No.
- Good.

08:47.099 --> 08:49.499
You should have seen
where this one girl hid hers.

08:53.072 --> 08:58.135
Come to find out that what I thought
was a boil on my neck...

08:58.310 --> 09:01.973
...was actually a carbuncle.

09:02.782 --> 09:04.647
Lovely.

09:04.817 --> 09:09.914
Little known fact, uh, carbuncles
are technically in the boil family.

09:10.089 --> 09:12.751
But it takes way longer to drain.

09:18.097 --> 09:20.964
- Charlie, help me here, I'm dying.
- No, you're doing fine.

09:21.133 --> 09:23.067
Tell her about your hemorrhoids.

09:23.969 --> 09:27.063
- Please, I'm begging you.
- All right.

09:27.239 --> 09:30.265
No sense letting my superpowers
go to waste.

09:30.443 --> 09:33.742
Ahem. So, Dr. Harper...

09:33.913 --> 09:37.280
...are we still going to Sun Valley
in your Gulfstream this weekend?

09:37.450 --> 09:40.044
You own your own trailer?

09:40.219 --> 09:42.312
No, no, that's an Airstream.

09:42.488 --> 09:44.285
Dr. Harper has a private jet.

09:45.024 --> 09:46.491
- Really?
- Oh, yeah.

09:46.659 --> 09:48.752
He needs one for his work.

09:48.928 --> 09:51.260
Hmm. What do you do?

09:51.430 --> 09:53.728
Uh, I am a chiropractor.

09:55.067 --> 09:58.002
A chiropractor without borders.

09:58.170 --> 10:01.401
He travels the world
adjusting the backs of starving children.

10:02.174 --> 10:08.113
Yes, you have to be, uh, very careful, um,
because their little bones are very brittle.

10:08.814 --> 10:11.442
Wow, you're amazing.

10:11.617 --> 10:14.586
No, it's just my job. Ha, ha.

10:15.054 --> 10:16.282
You're amazing.

10:16.956 --> 10:20.289
It wasn't tough. We had her at trailer.

10:21.427 --> 10:24.294
Another round on him.

10:55.828 --> 10:57.261
Uh-oh.

11:03.969 --> 11:05.368
Charlie.

11:05.538 --> 11:08.063
- Charlie.
- Go away, Alan.

11:08.240 --> 11:11.141
I really think
you need to wake up now.

11:11.310 --> 11:12.709
Shh.

11:12.878 --> 11:14.402
Chelsea's sleeping.

11:14.580 --> 11:18.016
Perhaps, but not here.

11:18.884 --> 11:23.253
Okay, what the hell is your prob...?

11:24.690 --> 11:26.681
Oh, dear.

11:28.661 --> 11:31.494
- What happened?
- I don't know.

11:31.664 --> 11:35.464
- Who is she?
- I don't know.

11:35.634 --> 11:37.602
What the hell do you know, Alan?

11:37.770 --> 11:43.265
I know we're in a strange woman's bed,
together, naked.

11:52.551 --> 11:55.179
- Let's get the hell out of here.
- Good idea.

11:58.490 --> 12:01.186
- You remember anything?
- I remember we were in Pavlov's.

12:01.360 --> 12:04.591
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.
You were hitting on some chick.

12:04.763 --> 12:06.628
Guess it worked.

12:07.132 --> 12:09.032
Do you happen to remember
how I did it?

12:09.201 --> 12:10.862
- Alan, focus.
- Okay, right, right.

12:11.036 --> 12:14.005
I think there was something about
a trailer in Sun Valley?

12:14.907 --> 12:16.636
Are we in Idaho?

12:18.544 --> 12:20.239
No mountains, no snow.

12:23.148 --> 12:25.776
Why are you wearing my underwear?

12:25.951 --> 12:29.819
- Why are you wearing mine?
- Oh, boy.

12:31.323 --> 12:32.483
Let's just go.

12:32.658 --> 12:34.785
Should we leave her a little note?

12:34.960 --> 12:37.428
- What?
- A thank-you, maybe my phone number.

12:37.596 --> 12:39.996
- Are you crazy? Just keep moving.
- But she's cute.

12:40.165 --> 12:43.566
- And I need a plus-one for your wedding.
- Oh, my God. My wedding.

12:43.736 --> 12:46.034
You're right, it could be awkward.

12:48.474 --> 12:50.135
What have I done, Alan?

12:50.309 --> 12:52.937
Less than 24 hours after I set a date
for my wedding...

12:53.112 --> 12:55.307
...I wake up in bed
with another woman.

12:55.481 --> 12:59.440
And me.
You woke up in bed with me too.

13:09.595 --> 13:12.621
- What the hell did we do last night?
- I wish I knew.

13:12.798 --> 13:15.164
- What am I gonna tell Chelsea?
- Well, let's think.

13:15.334 --> 13:17.461
I mean, maybe there's
an innocent explanation.

13:17.636 --> 13:19.399
Oh, really? And what might that be?

13:19.571 --> 13:22.768
- Clearly we all had a bit much to drink.
- Yeah.

13:22.942 --> 13:24.375
And you and I, being gentlemen...

13:24.543 --> 13:26.773
...escorted the lady home.
- Mm-hm.

13:26.946 --> 13:29.312
She invited us in for a cup of coffee
to sober up.

13:29.481 --> 13:32.279
Was that before
or after we switched underwear?

13:35.020 --> 13:36.248
Let me finish.

13:36.422 --> 13:40.222
Uh, so we went into her apartment and...

13:41.827 --> 13:44.159
I don't know
what you're gonna tell Chelsea.

13:44.330 --> 13:45.695
Here is what you tell her.

13:45.864 --> 13:50.324
Tell her you were detained by the secret
police, strip-searched and water boarded.

13:50.502 --> 13:52.595
Just drive.

13:53.005 --> 13:54.973
Worked for me.

13:57.810 --> 14:00.574
All right, here's what we're gonna do.

14:01.013 --> 14:03.072
We're gonna forget
this night ever happened.

14:03.248 --> 14:04.909
Good idea.

14:05.250 --> 14:07.741
Giddyup, horsy, giddyup.

14:11.690 --> 14:15.182
Of course,
that may be easier said than done.

14:26.238 --> 14:28.604
Great, no one's up yet.

14:28.774 --> 14:31.709
All right, go to bed. I'll see you later.

14:35.748 --> 14:37.181
- Charlie?
- What?

14:37.349 --> 14:38.680
You want your boxers back?

14:41.453 --> 14:43.546
- You keep them.
- Really? Gee, thanks.

14:46.392 --> 14:48.223
- Charlie, Charlie.
- Yeah?

14:48.394 --> 14:52.125
Uh, if I put them in the laundry, Berta will
wash them and give them back to you.

14:52.297 --> 14:54.231
Then hand-wash them.

14:54.400 --> 14:55.560
Of course.

14:58.170 --> 15:00.161
- Charlie, Charlie.
- What?

15:01.106 --> 15:04.200
- Woolite or a mild detergent?
- I don't care.

15:04.943 --> 15:07.309
No worries, I'll check the label.

15:08.313 --> 15:11.146
- Oh, Charlie.
- What?

15:11.316 --> 15:14.217
Thanks for taking me out with you.
I had a really good time.

15:43.949 --> 15:45.917
Charlie?

15:46.285 --> 15:48.719
- Yeah, babe?
- Are you just getting home?

15:48.887 --> 15:52.755
No, no. No, I was a little drunk,
so I slept downstairs for a while.

15:52.925 --> 15:54.256
I didn't wanna disturb you.

15:54.426 --> 15:56.121
Did you have a good time with Alan?

15:56.628 --> 15:59.563
Oh, come on, it was Alan.
How much fun could I have had?

16:01.066 --> 16:07.130
&lt;i>Happy birthday, Mr. President&lt;/i>

16:07.639 --> 16:12.702
&lt;i>Happy birthday to you&lt;/i>

16:14.580 --> 16:18.243
Oh, you don't mean that.
- No. Ha, ha. No.

16:18.417 --> 16:23.013
We had an okay time.
Pretty forgettable.

16:23.655 --> 16:27.955
I talked to my parents last night.
They are so excited.

16:28.127 --> 16:30.960
Not as excited as me.

16:33.999 --> 16:36.263
I'm gonna make you a great wife,
Charlie Harper.

16:36.435 --> 16:38.027
I know.

16:38.203 --> 16:43.641
And I'm gonna... cut down
on my drinking.

16:47.212 --> 16:48.679
Boy, I don't know, Chels.

16:48.847 --> 16:51.407
I really like the white roses
for the centerpieces.

16:51.583 --> 16:54.416
- You don't think it's too much?
- No, no.

16:54.586 --> 16:58.989
The rose symbolizes love
and white symbolizes, you know...

16:59.158 --> 17:01.524
...the cleanness of that love.

17:03.395 --> 17:05.192
- Cleanness?
- Yeah.

17:05.364 --> 17:09.698
Yeah, like purity or untainted by filth.

17:12.271 --> 17:15.206
A white rose is a rose you can trust.

17:15.374 --> 17:20.141
Making it the centerpiece is appropriate,
because you're my centerpiece.

17:20.312 --> 17:24.009
You know, the piece
that supersedes all other pieces.

17:25.717 --> 17:28.550
- Are you still drunk?
- Only with love.

17:31.356 --> 17:33.688
Oh, it's my grandmother.

17:34.226 --> 17:35.716
Hi, Grammy.

17:35.894 --> 17:39.057
Yeah, it's gonna be a June wedding.

17:39.831 --> 17:43.699
Excuse me.
That's a terrible thing to say, Grammy.

17:43.869 --> 17:46.861
Besides, I said June, not Jew.

17:56.848 --> 18:00.306
- Okay, what have you done?
- Beg your pardon?

18:00.485 --> 18:02.385
That sweet naive hick
you're marrying...

18:02.554 --> 18:06.183
...might buy this loving, cooperative
attitude, but not your mommy.

18:06.358 --> 18:08.918
Hey, can't a fella just be excited about
floral centerpieces?

18:09.094 --> 18:11.085
A gay fella.

18:11.997 --> 18:14.522
You're feeling guilty about something.
What is it?

18:14.700 --> 18:17.362
Nothing.
I've got nothing to feel guilty about.

18:20.105 --> 18:23.768
Okay, okay, okay.
Now you give him your underwear.

18:26.111 --> 18:29.376
- Charlie?
- I'm not really sure what I did.

18:29.548 --> 18:33.712
- So a drunken escapade?
- Is there another kind of escapade?

18:33.885 --> 18:36.786
Well, whatever you do,
don't tell Chelsea about it.

18:37.789 --> 18:42.920
Confession may be good for the soul,
but it's a hot lead enema to a marriage.

18:43.829 --> 18:49.028
I know, I know, but I've got these freaky
memory flashes and I feel so guilty.

18:49.201 --> 18:53.228
Trust me,
those memories will fade with time.

18:53.405 --> 18:54.531
How do you know?

18:54.706 --> 18:56.674
Let me tell you a story.

18:56.842 --> 19:00.073
Many years ago when I was married
to your second stepfather...

19:00.245 --> 19:01.576
The carpet king?

19:02.547 --> 19:05.607
Well, I called him that.
It wasn't his occupation.

19:07.019 --> 19:09.214
Anyway, he was away on business...

19:09.421 --> 19:12.913
...and you and your brother
were in summer camp or somewhere.

19:13.925 --> 19:15.324
And l...

19:15.827 --> 19:21.265
Well, I was lonely, bored,
and the circus was in town.

19:23.435 --> 19:25.960
And when I woke up in that Motel 6...

19:26.138 --> 19:30.666
...clown makeup smeared
all over my bosom, I was alone.

19:30.842 --> 19:33.640
The Chinese acrobats, the strong man,
the little people...

19:33.812 --> 19:35.302
...moved on to the next town.

19:35.480 --> 19:37.505
Oh, my God!

19:39.084 --> 19:41.575
- What did you do then?
- Well, what could I do?

19:41.753 --> 19:45.951
I showered,
plucked the sequins from my hoo-hoo...

19:46.792 --> 19:49.283
...held my head up
and got on with my life.

19:49.461 --> 19:51.486
And you never told the carpet king?

19:51.997 --> 19:56.093
No, of course not.
I loved him too much.

19:56.268 --> 20:00.329
Your second stepfather was the third
best thing that ever happened to me.

20:00.505 --> 20:01.870
Behind me and Alan?

20:03.408 --> 20:05.103
Sure.

20:08.513 --> 20:12.074
I think some teenagers
are fooling around under the deck again.

20:12.250 --> 20:13.274
Really?

20:13.485 --> 20:16.113
Yeah. Found a pair of men's briefs
by the side of the house.

20:17.422 --> 20:21.051
Damn kids. No respect for anything.

20:26.732 --> 20:30.566
Listen, Chels, we need to talk.

20:31.436 --> 20:34.997
- Something wrong?
- Yeah.

20:35.440 --> 20:36.498
What is it?

20:37.409 --> 20:40.242
I got these...
These pictures in my head.

20:40.412 --> 20:43.472
And I'm afraid if I don't tell you
about them...

20:43.648 --> 20:45.206
...they're gonna drive me crazy.

20:46.251 --> 20:47.548
Go ahead.

20:50.822 --> 20:53.154
Well, what happened was...

20:55.026 --> 20:58.757
My second stepfather went on a business
trip while the circus was in town.

20:59.931 --> 21:04.265
Alan and I were at camp
or someplace.

21:04.736 --> 21:07.534
And my mother was lonely.

21:31.329 --> 21:34.730
- Shouldn't we leave her a note?
- Just keep walking.
